# JES results in VNS
@scenario tutorial_lesson_50
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/50_jes_return.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt launch]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Open the postcard scene and choose a card. JES sends that card's name and stamp count back to this VNS scene.
@label lab
> Open the postcard scene -> demo
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label demo
# region launch
[clear card]
[clear stamp_count]
[jes push scripts/scenes/return_lab.jes label result]
# endregion
@label result
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/return_lab.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt returns]
[if card == "none"]
ginger: You left without a card. Esc returned a stamp count of ${stamp_count}.
[else]
ginger: Your card is from the ${card}. The stamp count came back as ${stamp_count}.
[endif]
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[clear card]
[clear stamp_count]
[if !tutorial_done_50]
[flag tutorial_done_50]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_10]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Give the waterfront postcard three stamps. Which file owns the value that VNS receives?
> The JES scene that returns stamp_count. -> practice_result
> The VNS dialogue that displays stamp_count. -> practice_hint
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: VNS substitutes the value from the return action. Find the binding for key 2.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: Update key 2's return block, then pick Waterfront again to check the result.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Where does VNS resume after the postcard scene returns?
> At the result label named in the push command. -> correct
> At the first label of the tutorial hub. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
ginger: The push command names a return label in the calling scene.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: Yes. The return action closes JES, copies its payload into VNS variables, and resumes the lesson at result.
> Replay example -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
